sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-goals-03> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In the evolved neural cellular automaton, tissues selected only to self-organize the French flag within 100 steps could restore the target pattern after perturbations applied later (e.g. converting two columns of the red stripe to white at step 110), although they failed after very large perturbations such as converting the whole red stripe.";
    dc:type "simulation-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Evolved tissues repair perturbed patterns although repair was never selected for";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Pio-Lopez L, Bischof J, LaPalme JV, Levin M, “The scaling of goals from cellular to anatomical homeostasis: an evolutionary simulation, experiment and analysis”, Interface focus (2023), doi:10.1098/rsfs.2022.0072; section “Computational results › The tissue is robust to perturbation”. Scope: In silico 2D neural cellular automata evolved for the French flag problem"
}
